@startuml 04-sequence-cli-print
title Printing from the command line (x3print.py)
autonumber

actor User as U
participant "x3print.py" as CLI
participant "render pipeline" as R
participant "X3Printer" as P
participant "printer X3" as X3

U -> CLI : x3print.py text "Hello"
CLI -> R : render_text(text, width, size, ...)
R -> R : threshold / dithering / rotation
R --> CLI : 1-bit image (500 dots wide)
CLI -> CLI : _embed() into the 864 dot raster
CLI -> P : X3Printer(mac=...)
CLI -> P : connect()

alt MAC unknown
  P -> P : detect_mac() via bluetoothctl
end
P -> X3 : 0x80 token / init
P -> X3 : 0x0a speed (0x55)
P -> X3 : 0x09 density (0x0c)
loop every 432 bytes = 4 rows
  P -> X3 : 0x00 raster frame
end
P -> X3 : 0x02 feed (200 steps)
note over P, X3
  The whole job goes out in one continuous stream,
  without pauses between the blocks: a gap would let the
  printer's buffer run empty and stop the motor in the
  middle of a page.  The RFCOMM flow control blocks the
  writes while the printer works off its buffer.
end note
P -> X3 : 0x10 status query (queued behind the job)
X3 --> P : reply = everything was read, closing is safe
P -> P : close()
CLI --> U : "Print job sent ..."
@enduml
